Falsifies `system_tests::user::network_tests::an_accept_nobody_answers_ends_at_the_stacks_bound`.

Architecture: aarch64 (the hunk is portable userspace code in `net_stack`; the riscv64 twin, `riscv_virtio_tests`, falls to the same patch, and x86_64 has no such test)

The defect is `service_until` handing `wait_for_nic` no deadline, which is the tree before
2026-10-13 (UTC): with no smoltcp timer pending, a virtio wait blocks on the interrupt alone, so a
listener nobody connects to never sees its 15 s bound.

Expected to fail: no assertion; the test's `ipc_receive` never returns and the kernel watchdog
fires, "WATCHDOG: no progress for ~60 s. Every core idle, every thread blocked". Confirmed red on
2026-10-13 (UTC) on both riscv64 and aarch64 with `cargo xtask test --arch <arch> --test
an_accept_nobody_answers_ends_at_the_stacks_bound`; green with the fix in 15.08 s and 15.06 s.

diff --git a/components/src/socket_operations.rs b/components/src/socket_operations.rs
index f3df0472c..4fec0757f 100644
--- a/components/src/socket_operations.rs
+++ b/components/src/socket_operations.rs
@@ -27,7 +27,7 @@ pub(crate) fn service_until(
             iface.poll(instant(), dev, sockets);
             return cond(sockets);
         }
-        wait_for_nic(iface, dev, sockets, Some(deadline));
+        wait_for_nic(iface, dev, sockets, None);
     }
 }
 
